#
# Conformance case: transaction/trajectory-audit (T6, issue #716).
#
# The READ-ONLY trajectory audit at the corpus level. The world facts (input.nq) record a
# gmeow:ToolCall SEQUENCE — the memory MCP triad's store_claim then revise_belief — NOT an
# authored transaction-program combinator. The native auditor
# (crates/logic/src/transaction/trajectory.rs) discovers the bound ToolCalls
# (logic:instantiatesSchema), groups them under their logic:properPartOf anchor (which bears
# the logic:transitionFromState start state), orders them by gmeow:atTime, right-folds them
# into a logic:SerialConjunction, and runs the SAME executional-entailment engine as the
# authored transaction cases — verifying pre/postconditions and atomicity with no write-back
# to the recorded calls.
#
# The anchor runs under logic:HypotheticalExecution (a governing logic:ReasoningContract in
# input.nq), so the verdict is recorded with a single content-addressed
# logic:executedHypotheticallyAs witness and the committed effect substrate is SUPPRESSED —
# "would this recorded continuation reach the goal?" answered without committing it. The
# anchor names a logic:planGoal whose logic:planGoalSituation (claimSuppressed) the trajectory
# reaches, so the audit emits the goal-reachability verdict by reusing the EXISTING flat
# gmeow:satisfiedBy projection — which (correctly) discloses the lossy goal-evaluation collapse,
# flipping runtime preservation to SoundUnder.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this input.logic.ttl
# carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/trajectory-audit/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the Evolution facet that classifies the audited
# transaction. logic:TransactionPathEvolution drives certification to the transaction-path
# decidability class (conflict-serializability; PTIME classification, not search). The contract
# also declares logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution for fidelity with the
# world-facts wiring that drives the sandbox emission.
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution ;
    logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution .
